# Third-party UI reference screenshots: excluded from the public repository
refs/

# Worker folders, and anything else that appears at the root.
#
# Divixi's "a folder each" worker mode gives a worker its own folder directly
# under the track folder -- which, when you develop Divixi with Divixi, is this
# repository root -- named after the worker itself
# (own_dir() in src-tauri/src/conductor.rs). The name is whatever the worker is
# called, so there is no prefix or parent folder to match on, and a new worker
# adds a new root-level folder at any time. Rather than list names that go stale,
# ignore every directory at the root and name the ones that belong to the project.
#
# Root-level FILES are deliberately left alone: a new LICENSE or CONTRIBUTING.md
# still shows up in git status. Only directories are covered.
#
# Adding a real top-level directory to the project? Add a "!" line for it here,
# or git will not see it.
/*/
!/.github/
!/crates/
!/docs/
!/scripts/
!/src-tauri/
!/ui/
